# Tag 1.4.0 (quay, measured 2026-08-24): python 3.12.14, pandas 3.0.5, numpy 2.5.2,
# polars 1.43.2, NO pyarrow and no fastparquet. Parquet under this env therefore goes
# through polars, which carries its own reader and writer; `lib::fabfos_evidence` exposes
# `read_parquet` / `write_parquet` and picks the engine the interpreter has, since
# that module is also imported outside any container, where pyarrow is what exists.
# Nothing under this env may reach parquet by another route -- `pd.read_parquet`
# and `DataFrame.to_parquet` are pyarrow front ends and fail here.
#
# A bare tag bump is a silent dependency rewrite for every transform naming this
# env, and it is not announced by the version number: 1.3.1 (== sha256:334b01e4...)
# is an OLDER build than 1.2.5 and carries no polars at all. Verify the imports in
# the image.
container: docker://quay.io/hallamlab/python_for_data_science:1.4.0
conda: python_for_data_science
